Hi all,

I would like to remove the too much white space between bars of the attached bar plot.   But, I could not remove this.  I followed several solutions posted on stack overflow and in this google forum as well- nothing worked.  My graph is generated from metagenomics data.  Here's the code I originally used to generate this graph:

ggplot(data = psmelt(ps.taxa_rarefy_control_CR_JAX_TAC_hi_abundant), mapping = aes_string(x = "vendor", y = "Abundance")) +
  geom_bar(aes(color=Family, fill=Family), stat="identity", position="fill", width = 0.2) + theme_bw() +
  theme(panel.border = element_blank(), panel.grid.major = element_blank(), panel.grid.minor = element_blank(), axis.line = element_line(colour = "black"), legend.position = "bottom") + xlab("   ") +
  guides(color = guide_legend(nrow=6)) +
  scale_x_discrete(expand = c(0, 0))

I will greatly appreciate if you please let me know how can I remove the space between CR, JAX and TAC bars.   I also tried the binwidth=0 within ggplot function, but it didn't work.

Thanks,

Saif

From u27405c4b711a1080 at groups.google.com  Wed Jul 18 14:59:16 2018
