MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Saif,

I think there are two issues.

1. you're specifying the width of the bars at 0.2, this will make your bars 20% of the width of the space. This makes them nice and narrow like you have above.
2. The second issue is that your legend is super large because of the names. That is stretching the plot out to fit it on the same window.

Here's an example:

library(tidyverse)

DF <- read.table(text="Rank ReallySuperDuperlongname1     ReallySuperDuperlongname2     ReallySuperDuperlongname3

1    500    250    50

2    400    100    30

3    300    155    100

4    200    90     10", header=TRUE)

# this is close to what you have

DF %>%

gather(., trait, value, -Rank) %>%

ggplot(., aes(x = Rank, y = value, fill = trait)) +

geom_bar(stat = "identity", position="fill", width = 0.2) +

theme_bw() +

theme(panel.border = element_blank(), panel.grid.major = element_blank(), panel.grid.minor = element_blank(), axis.line = element_line(colour = "black"), legend.position = "bottom") +

xlab("   ") +

guides(color = guide_legend(nrow = 2)) +

scale_x_discrete(expand = c(0, 0))

# if you change the width to 0.9 (the default) you get fat bars that fill the space

DF %>%

gather(., trait, value, -Rank) %>%

ggplot(., aes(x = Rank, y = value, fill = trait)) +

geom_bar(stat = "identity", position="fill", width = 0.9) +

theme_bw() +

theme(panel.border = element_blank(), panel.grid.major = element_blank(), panel.grid.minor = element_blank(), axis.line = element_line(colour = "black"), legend.position = "bottom") +

xlab("   ") +

guides(color = guide_legend(nrow = 2)) +

scale_x_discrete(expand = c(0, 0))

To fix the first issue, take the width argument out of the geom_bar() call. Or specify the default (0.9) as Above.

Regarding the legend, if you want to keep the width narrow but need that size of legend, I think you might have to extract the legend from the plot and use cowplot, patchwork, or gridExtra to patch it back together.

HTH,
Brandon

